\f0\b\fs38 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Welcome to MenuMeters 3.1.0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 MenuMeters shows CPU, disk, memory, and network activity in the macOS menu bar. It supports Apple Silicon and Intel Macs running macOS 26 or later.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf0 Automatic updates\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 MenuMeters checks for updates once a day and asks before installing one. It installs only updates signed with this fork's key. To turn the daily check off, or to check now, use the Updates controls below. Each check downloads a small feed from salamacchine.it. It sends the version of MenuMeters, and nothing about your Mac.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf0 What's new in 3.1.0\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The CPU meter shows the real load. Before, it read close to 100% all the time.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Temperatures work again on Intel Macs.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The process list includes system and other users' processes, and stays current while the menu is open.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The network menu updates while it is open, and no longer runs a shell to read link speeds.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The disk menu no longer lists hidden system volumes, and reports a failed eject.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The memory menu shows the right cache hit rate and memory pressure.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 MenuMeters adds itself to the login items on first launch only. Change it with the Startup checkbox below.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

